[Music]  disney's live-action version of mulan  is not a shot-for-shot remake of the  animated classic from 1998  instead it's more of a reimagining based  on the ancient chinese poem  the ballad of mulan and while so many  things are different the heart of the  story is still there  along with plenty of nods to the  animated original here are all the ways  disney's live-action mulan  is different from the original oh and  warning spoilers ahead  when the new movie starts mulan is a  child and we watch her grow older on  screen  but in the original we see her at only  one age for the duration of the film  mulan's surname is tweaked from faw  the cantonese pronunciation of her name  to hua which makes it truer to the name  of the original ballad  however both names have the same basic  meaning later when mulan needs to come  up with a fake name for the army  she settles on hua joon as opposed to  pha ping from the original movie  it's ping ping there are also some  changes to mulan's family in the  live-action version she now has a  younger sister  in the animated version she's an only  child though she does have a dog named  little brother  while in some versions of the original  legend she's an only child  there are other versions where she has  siblings also missing from the  live-action version  mulan's quirky grandmother thanks to the  film's longer running time they were  able to more fully flesh out the bond  between mulan and her father  in the new version mulan carries her  father's sword with the words  royal brave true etched into the blade  the phrase is repeated throughout the  film  speaking to the theme of the story loyal  brave  true but take a look at the sword in the  animated version  you'll notice both sides of it are  completely blank another iconic object  from the original movie  remains unchanged boulon's hair clip  with a flower on it  in both movies she leaves it behind to  signify that she's left home  in the animated movie she leaves it by  her parents bed in the live-action one  she leaves it in her father's wardrobe  but there were some elements from the  animated movie  that just would not have worked as well  in live action specifically  mulan's anthropomorphic animal sidekicks  like ricky the lucky cricket  qrikey was a crucial part of the  matchmaking scene and the troublemaking  bug causes chaos after soaking in a cup  of tea  in the reimagining instead of a cricket  a spider pops up on the table mulan  tries to cover it with a teapot  ultimately ending in disaster pricky may  not be in the movie  but he is there in spirit one of mulan's  fellow human soldiers is named cricket  and like kricky he's called a good luck  charm  yep this cricket's a lucky one another  fan favorite and a controversial  character missing from the film  mushu the dragon who was voiced by eddie  murphy you might recall that the  wisecracking creature  served as mulan's guardian sent by her  ancestors while mushu was popular with  u.s audiences  chinese viewers found him to be  trivializing so no mushu means no scene  where he shatters the dragon guardian  statue that is actually supposed to  accompany mulan  instead it's mulan who accidentally  shatters a statue  that of a phoenix the phoenix makes  sense as a mushu stand-in and not just  because the two creatures have a similar  look  after she leaves for war mulan's father  prays to the ancestors and the phoenix  to protect her so while there are no  actual ghosts of ancestors seen here  we still know they have mulan's back and  the phoenix follows her silently  throughout her journey  other characters from the animated  version are present here but with new  names  instead of shan yu the leader of the  invading northern army  is bori khan and he has more motivations  now than just wanting to conquer china  khan also wants to avenge his father's  death bori khan is fighting with the  rurons  not the huns as shanyu was in the  original  this might be more accurate some  historians have said the huns were  likely more focused on attacking europe  than china during mulan's time  alongside bori khan is a completely new  villain to the universe  named xinyon in the animated movie  shanyu does have a falcon  which also acts as his spy but the  falcon never takes the form of a person  according to the filmmakers they wanted  to bring in a new female antagonist as a  way to balance out the protagonist see  both characters are able to harness the  power of qi  concept that is never mentioned in the  original it's apparent that mulan can do  this early in the film  and later on it allows her to do  everything from jump across rooftops to  scale walls  another one of the animated characters  wasn't necessarily removed but rather  divided up  according to the producer jason reed lee  shang the captain who notably got down  to business  was split into two separate characters  one is commander tong  mulan's mentor and the other is a fellow  soldier named huang hui who grows close  to mulan reed also said it didn't feel  appropriate having an older commanding  officer be her love interest  in an interview with insider animated  mulan co-director tony bancroft  said that they actually considered  making li shang mulan's equal  originally they had another character as  the sergeant who would have turned out  to be a spy once that character was cut  li shang got a promotion one of the most  iconic parts of the animated mulan  is missing from this live-action version  the songs instead of making the film a  musical  memorable lines from the songs are woven  into the dialogue  for example mulan says yes it's best i  will bring honor to us all calling back  to the song  honor to us all and while you won't get  to hear donnie osmond saying  i'll make a man out of you the sergeant  does tell the young warriors we're gonna  make men out of every single one of you  at one point mulan sits at a table with  some fellow soldiers who talk about  their favorite characteristics in a  woman  ling holds up a drawing of a woman he'd  been matched with that looks similar to  those sketches from the animated scene  poe then says i don't care what she  looks like i care what she cooks like  which is very similar to a lion sung by  chen po  in a girl worth fighting for and while  mulan never sings the words herself  the tune for reflection can be heard on  the score during several brilliant  moments throughout the film  while the basics of the story are the  same some major plot points have also  been altered  in the animated movie the toughest  obstacle the commander throws of the  soldiers is making them retrieve an  arrow from the top of a high pole  while holding a pair of weights in the  live-action movie they also must carry  full buckets of water to the top of the  high mountain  in the animated training montage they do  train with buckets but it's large sacks  they're carrying up a mountain  in both movies mulan is injured but in  different ways  in the new movie she's hit by one of  shinyan's throwing stars but in the  animated movie  she's slashed by sean u's blade which  ultimately leads to her being stripped  in a medical tent  and revealed as a woman one of the most  dramatic moments in mulan's story is  when her secret is revealed  the live-action version has her being  the one to make the decision to out  herself as a woman  in the middle of battle she lets down  her hair and shows her true self  it's an especially empowering moment  that gives the character more agency  this scene also might explain why the  live-action version doesn't show mulan  chopping her long hair off earlier with  her father's blade  this battle is brought to an abrupt end  by a huge avalanche a famous scene from  the animated movie that director nikki  cairo decided to keep in the live-action  film  but instead of shooting a cannon in the  new movie mulan tricks boricon's men  into firing a large boulder at the  mountain  and nobody is seen rising from the snow  on skates this time around there's no  victory parade in the city and while  shaun you met an unfortunate  firework-related demise in the animated  movie  boricon tumbles to the ground before  mulan finishes him off with one of his  own arrows  and if you were waiting for fireworks  that doesn't happen until mulan saves  the emperor who  played by actor jet li has a much more  active role in this film  venturing out to fight his enemy when  mulan returns home in the live-action  version  her father says it is my daughter that  means everything to me  in the animated version after handing  him gifts from the emperor he says  something different but with the same  general intent  the greatest gift and honor is having  you for a daughter when mulan gets a  visit from commander tong it's not a  romantic gesture  rather he comes with a new sword as  mulan's was destroyed during the final  battle and a second invitation from the  emperor to become an  officer in the emperor's guard in the  ballad the animated movie  and the live-action movie the emperor  asked mulan to come work for him  mulan always declines choosing instead  to return  home the film ends before she can give  an answer but it would make sense if she  wanted to fight again  because in the ballad mulan and her  comrades traveled together for 12 years  were there any other big differences you  spotted between the animated and the  live-action films  let us know in the comments

